# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
vision_examples/build/
vision_examples/bin/
*.o

# colcon, for the ROS 2 packages of chapter 18
build/
install/
log/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python environments and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights the examples download or export
#
# Not versioned: they are large and download_model.sh / export_model.py bring
# them back.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/models/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whatever the examples write when they run
#
# Every example runs from its own directory and writes there, so the pattern is
# anchored to the two levels of the example tree, <chapter>/<example>/. It has
# to be: an earlier version anchored these to the repository root and therefore
# never matched anything, and running the examples left the tree dirty.
#
# Matching by extension rather than by name is deliberate, so that a new output
# is covered without touching this file. It is safe here because only .cpp,
# Makefile, CMakeLists.txt, .sh and .py are versioned inside an example
# directory. The same pattern without the numeric prefixes would reach
# data/aruco/*.yml and .github/workflows/*.yml, which must stay visible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.ply
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.pcd
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.yml
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.yaml
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.xml
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.png
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.jpg
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.avi
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.mp4
[0-9][0-9]_*/[0-9][0-9]_*/*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and local tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired material
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
old/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The binary each example builds
#
# Building an example on its own leaves the binary next to its sources, named
# after its own directory. gitignore cannot express "a file named like the
# directory that holds it", and it cannot match "no extension" either, so the
# list below is explicit.
#
# That is the safer failure mode: forget an entry and the new binary shows up
# as untracked, which is visible. A whitelist of source extensions would fail
# the other way, hiding a new kind of source file without a word.
#
# Add a line when you add an example, or build from the root CMakeLists, which
# puts every binary in vision_examples/bin/ instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*/02_01_read_image/02_01_read_image
/*/02_02_color_spaces/02_02_color_spaces
/*/02_03_mat_copy_roi/02_03_mat_copy_roi
